From b97b09e32cdab2dd8eadb65d1a6d66313247117f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:28:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] acpi_gpio_events: ACPI GPIO-signalled events on PL061;
 acpi_button on arm64

Apple's Virtualization.framework and QEMU's virt machine signal the power
button as an ACPI GPIO event: the ARMH0061 (PL061) device's _AEI names the
pin, and its _Exx/_Lxx method does Notify(PWRB, 0x80). The new driver binds
to ARMH0061, parses _CRS and _AEI, programs the event pins, and evaluates the
pin's method from a kernel thread on interrupt. acpi_button, now built for
arm64 too, turns the notification into /dev/power/button/power, and
power_daemon shuts the system down. A VM stop request now ends in a clean
Haiku shutdown within about a second.

The private acpi.h gains the GPIO connection resource (ACPICA's packed
layout) and its constants. Only the registers Linux's pl061 driver touches
are written, and only the event pins' bits: Virtualization.framework's
PL061 model terminates the VM on writes it does not expect (AFSEL, or IC
bits of unconfigured pins).
---
